---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy | Pro UPI QR";
const description = "Learn which Pro UPI QR tools stay local, what cloud QR and checkout data is stored, retention periods, providers, and deletion options.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 md:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="rounded-[14px] border border-forest/10 bg-white p-6 shadow-md md:p-10">
      <a href="/" class="text-sm font-bold text-leaf hover:underline">&larr; Back to Generator</a>
      
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-forest md:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-forest/50">Last Updated: October 12, 2026</p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-forest/80">
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">1. Scope</h2>
          <p>
            This policy explains which Pro UPI QR features run entirely in your browser and which optional account or cloud features send limited data to our service providers. We minimize collection and do not ask for a UPI PIN, banking password, card number, or OTP.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">2. Local-First Tools</h2>
          <p>
            Static QR generators, printable documents, calculators, image tools, and decoders normally process their form data and uploaded files inside your browser. That content is not uploaded to Pro UPI QR. A generated <code>upi://pay</code> link opens a UPI app; Pro UPI QR does not receive your UPI PIN or process the resulting bank transaction.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">3. Browser Storage and Optional Groq Requests</h2>
          <p>
            Many tools save drafts in localStorage on your device. The payments workspace at /app/ (payment tracker) keeps your business details, clients, invoices, payments, and reminder history there too; it is not uploaded unless you sign in to sync (section 4). Clearing site data removes all of it, so use the workspace's backup download. Bank statement files you import into the tracker are read inside your browser and never uploaded; only the payments you choose to record are saved. The menu tool can optionally call Groq directly from your browser using an API key you provide; when you use that option, the key is kept in browser storage and your menu prompt is sent directly to Groq under Groq's terms. It is not routed through or stored by our server.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">4. Accounts and Dynamic QR Campaigns</h2>
          <p>
            Clerk processes account identity, authentication cookies, and session data for sign-in and dashboard features. Merchant profiles store an account identifier, merchant name, UPI ID, and secret API credential in Vercel KV. For a dynamic QR campaign, we store the account identifier, server-generated campaign ID, title, HTTPS or UPI destination, category, optional expiry date, pause state, and aggregate mobile/desktop scan counts. The destination is disclosed when someone follows that campaign's QR. Individual scan histories and precise locations are not retained by the campaign service.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Payments workspace sync (optional).</strong> If you sign in on the payment tracker, your workspace — business name, UPI ID, phone, GSTIN and Udyam number you entered, client names and contact details, invoice numbers, amounts, dates, descriptions, payments with any UTR you typed, and reminder timestamps — is stored in Vercel KV under a hashed account key so it can sync between your devices. Reminder messages themselves are not stored; WhatsApp and SMS open on your device. The cloud copy stays until you choose Settings → Delete cloud copy or ask us to delete your account. Deleting the cloud copy does not erase the copy saved in your browser.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Pay links.</strong> When you create a pay link for an invoice, anyone with the link can see your business name, UPI ID, the invoice number, description, due date, and the amount still due. The page never shows your client's name or contact details. A Pro statement link for a client shows, instead of one invoice, the number, dates, and amount due of each of that client's unpaid invoices and the total — never descriptions, names, or contact details. We store the link's random token with a hashed account key and invoice reference until you turn the link off. If a payer submits "I've paid", we store the UTR they typed, an optional amount, and the time until you confirm or dismiss it; a submitted UTR is never treated as proof of payment. Pro UPI QR never receives or holds the money — payments go directly to your UPI ID.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Pro subscriptions.</strong> Pro is sold through Dodo Payments, our merchant of record: Dodo runs the checkout, takes the payment, handles GST, and issues your invoice, so we never receive your card number or UPI PIN. To create your Dodo customer record we share your account's email address and name with Dodo. We store your Dodo customer and subscription IDs, plan interval, subscription status, current period end, whether you cancelled, the end date of a free trial, and whether the account has had a subscription (so the free trial is offered once), under a hashed account key, plus webhook event IDs for seven days to ignore duplicate notifications. Dodo keeps payment and tax records under its own privacy policy and legal obligations.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Reminder notifications (optional).</strong> If you turn them on, we store your browser's push subscription (an endpoint URL issued by your browser's push service, such as Google, Apple, or Mozilla, and its encryption keys) under your hashed account key, for up to five devices. Each morning our server reads your synced workspace to build a short summary — how many invoices to chase, the overdue total, and the top client and amount — and sends it encrypted end to end, so the push service cannot read it. When a client submits a UTR on one of your pay links, we also send an immediate notification with the invoice number, any amount they entered, and the last four digits of the UTR. Notifications appear on your device, including the lock screen. Turn it off in the tracker's Settings or your browser; expired subscriptions are deleted automatically.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">5. Checkout and Payment-Response Data</h2>
          <p>
            Merchant checkout sessions store the merchant name and UPI ID, order reference, amount in paise, safe return URL, status, and any transaction reference submitted by the customer. A submitted reference is marked pending until the merchant confirms it. Checkout sessions expire after 24 hours. The separately signed payment-response API may retain order status, transaction reference, amount, and provider for 90 days in Vercel KV.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="early-access" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">6. Early-Access List</h2>
          <p>
            After you download or share a document from the invoice, receipt, quotation, proforma, or payment-reminder tools, or download a UPI QR code, we may show a card for the free payment tracker with an optional email list for launch news of features still in development, such as automatic WhatsApp reminders. Joining is never required to use any tool. If you join, we store only your email address, the tool you were using, your page language, whether you agreed to answer a few follow-up questions, and the sign-up date, in Vercel KV. Nothing from the document or QR code itself is sent. We use the address only to tell you when those features launch and, if you opted in, to ask those questions. We do not sell or share it. Each entry is deleted automatically 12 months after sign-up, or earlier on request.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="mcp" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">7. AI Assistant Connector (MCP)</h2>
          <p>
            If you add our MCP server at https://www.proupiqr.in/mcp/ to Claude or another AI app, that app sends our server the values each tool needs, such as a UPI ID, payee name, amount, note, upi:// link, error code, or dates. We use them only to compute the reply and then discard them: they are not stored in a database or written to our logs. We keep one daily total of tool calls with no identifiers, and a hashed network-address counter that expires after one minute to stop abuse (calls from Claude's shared Anthropic addresses share one such counter). The AI app's provider (for example, Anthropic for Claude) handles your conversation under its own privacy terms. Links the connector returns carry payment details after the # in the address, which your browser does not send to our server; they also carry a fixed utm_source=mcp tag, with nothing about you in it, so our analytics can count visits that came from AI apps. See <a href="/mcp-server/" class="text-leaf underline font-semibold">how the connector works</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">8. Hosting, Security, and Technical Logs</h2>
          <p>
            Vercel hosts the site and server functions and may process standard request information such as IP address, user agent, timestamps, and error logs under its own privacy terms. We use short-lived hashed request fingerprints for abuse rate limits; the rate-limit keys expire with their configured windows. Clerk and Groq process data only for the features described above.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">9. Retention and Deletion</h2>
          <p>
            Dynamic campaigns remain until their owner deletes them or we remove them for abuse. Checkout sessions expire after 24 hours, and signed payment-response records expire after 90 days. Early-access entries expire 12 months after sign-up. Synced workspaces remain until you delete the cloud copy or your account; pay links remain until you turn them off, and payer claims until you confirm or dismiss them. Merchant account settings remain while the account is active. To request account, merchant-profile, or early-access deletion, email us from the address you used. Provider security logs follow the provider's retention policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">10. Analytics, Advertising, and External Links</h2>
          <p>
            We do not run Google Analytics or Google AdSense. Vercel Speed Insights records cookie-free Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS) for the page, not form contents. Vercel Web Analytics records page views and named product events such as QR generated, PNG/PDF export, share, copy, tool error, early-access card viewed, joined, or dismissed, and payment-tracker invoice added, payment recorded, or reminder opened. Those events include only an action name and a short tool slug. They never include a VPA, payee name, amount, invoice text, or uploaded file. Our server also keeps daily aggregate counts, such as how many visits downloaded something from a free tool or opened the payment tracker (each visit counted once), how many pay links were created, or how many Pro checkouts started, with no account, device, or personal identifiers attached. Links to UPI apps, affiliate merchants, or other websites leave Pro UPI QR and are governed by those services.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-forest">11. Contact and Data Requests</h2>
          <p>
            For privacy questions, access requests, deletion requests, or corrections, email <a href="mailto:privacy@proupiqr.in" class="text-leaf underline font-semibold">privacy@proupiqr.in</a>. Include only the information needed to locate your account; never email a UPI PIN, OTP, or banking password.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
